<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan sugar output reaches 2.367 mln tonnes.</title>
<headline>Pakistan sugar output reaches 2.367 mln tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Pakistan Sugar Mills Association said on Thursday sugar production had reached 2.367 million tonnes by April 30 compared to 2.439 million tonnes at the same time a year ago.</p>
<p>It said mills aimed to produce 2.38 million tonnes in 1996/97, compared to 2.47 million in 1995/96 and 3.0 million in 1994/95.</p>
<p>Dealers bought 1.26 million tonnes, or 53.23 percent, of the production and the remaining 1.10 million tonnes, or 46.77 percent was at the mills.</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
